{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"jarl/proofs/log-boundary/Proofs.lean","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T08:27:44.591904Z","id":"c98018c0ee4103d12f59719574aa509076e08f348e1da1e1fbc53bce62a037e9","body":{"detail":"last_empty requires `state.lengths [\"len\"] = 0`, and last_final_slot requires slot len-1 to be `some`. README.md:151-152 and the coverage.json note for State::last say 'an empty retained prefix returns the base'. No theorem covers len > 0 with all retained slots None, or a None at len-1 after earlier entries, where Rust's `entries().next_back()` (src/state.rs:94) skips holes. State::truncate calls last() on every iteration (src/state.rs:161), so malformed-buffer reasoning there depends on this case.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":125},"end":{"line":155},"content_hash":"6a00499fe01d70acd5a996e2f4ea88802af11e636bc1857ea060f3e3add22ae8"},"suggested_fix":"Add a general theorem: last returns the id of the last `some` slot in `take len`, or the base when there is none. Alternatively, narrow the README and coverage wording to the two proven cases.","summary":"State::last is characterized only for len = 0 and for an occupied final slot, not for an empty retained prefix with len > 0 or for a trailing hole","tags":["review","review:2026-10-07-deep","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"jarl/proofs/log-boundary/Proofs.lean","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T10:08:39.037861Z","id":"ec9b16dddc1a91b01abf9c6efdb9cc4da29fbc906265157c3628327d54916fbf","body":{"detail":"log-boundary/Proofs.lean:125 last_empty requires state.lengths [\"len\"] = 0. :138 last_final_slot requires slots = front ++ [some entry] ++ suffix with len = front.length + 1. No theorem covers len > 0 with every retained slot None, or a None at len-1. src/state.rs:94 uses entries().next_back(), which skips holes, and src/state.rs:161 calls last() in truncate's loop. README.md:150-152 and the coverage.json:6543 note say 'empty retained prefix returns base', which is broader than len = 0. The storage Shape invariant rules out holes below len, so suggestion is the right severity.","kind":"comment","references":"c98018c0ee4103d12f59719574aa509076e08f348e1da1e1fbc53bce62a037e9","summary":"confirmed: State::last is proven only for len = 0 and for an occupied final slot","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
